  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining System Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the core requirements for the management system. Replacing \"SH Oficina\" necessitates a detailed feature analysis. I am evaluating functionalities to ensure comprehensive coverage, including scheduling, inventory, invoicing, and reporting. I am also working to capture the distinct needs of MGV Tecnologia e Assist\303\252ncia T\303\251cnica.\n\n\n**Clarifying Integration Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving into the system\'s architecture, specifically the tech stack. I\'m focusing on the frontend (React, TailwindCSS), backend (Node.js with Express), and Supabase for database and authentication. I\'m also planning to integrate with Bling\'s API for billing. I need to make the application fully functional out of the box within the specified environment. There seems to be confusion regarding Supabase integration; I need to clarify if it is an option as per instructions.\n\n\n**Assessing Backend Integration**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the backend integration strategy given the constraints. Since there are no live Supabase credentials, the plan shifts. I need to deliver a dual-mode, self-contained solution. I must offer a simulated Supabase experience alongside the Firebase/Cloud SQL option, given the user specified Supabase in their updated spec document. This allows me to implement a robust full-stack solution.\n\n\n**Implementing Mock Integrations**\n\nI\'m now implementing mock integrations to allow immediate user interaction. I\'m focusing on simulating Supabase and Bling functionalities for a seamless experience. This involves creating mock clients, models, OS, faturamento, and enabling features like DANFE download and SEFAZ error handling. I\'m also including Kanban drag-and-drop functionality for intuitive workflow management. I\'m following platform guidelines regarding API key configuration but will investigate the potential for a settings panel if requested by the user.\n\n\n**Evaluating User Management**\n\nI\'m now incorporating multi-user functionality, focusing on OAuth and workspace integrations. I am ensuring that the authentication and identity management from Sprint 1 are complete. I have also evaluated the relevance of the Gemini API for potential AI-driven features, but I\'m prioritizing user intent and omitting AI, adhering to the specifications of the user\'s initial request. I am also working on adding the new required Sprint 2 and 3 features.\n\n\n**Refining Fiscal Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating external fiscal systems. I\'m focusing on Bling\'s API for automated billing upon status updates, with robust error handling and simulated sandbox mode if credentials are absent, including SEFAZ rejections, DANFE generation and interactive logs. I\'m also ensuring role-based permissions, such as preventing an Editor from deleting records. I\'m also now planning connection monitoring for offline states. Finally, I\'m checking `metadata.json` for app naming as \"MGV Tecnologia - Gest\303\243o de Assist\303\252ncia T\303\251cnica\".\n\n\n**Constructing Backend Infrastructure**\n\nI\'m now focused on the backend setup; I\'ve analyzed the initial file tree and realized I must create `/server.ts` to build the Node.js Express backend. My plan is to implement a clean Express server. I\'ll make it serve as a backend proxy, allowing in-memory storage or local JSON file saving. This keeps it simple and robust, avoiding the need for a full database setup by default, allowing the software to run out-of-the-box.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
