  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning Application Architecture**\n\nI\'ve successfully installed all necessary packages. My focus has shifted towards application architecture and breaking down features into manageable Sprints. For Sprint 1, I\'m prioritizing user authentication and identity management using Supabase Auth. I\'ll start with a registration screen, either as a standalone page or embedded within our app layout.\n\n\n**Refining Feature Breakdown**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the login screen (`/login`) and active session handling. Upon successful login, I\'ll obtain a JWT token and redirect to the dashboard. The user metadata in Supabase Auth will determine the employee\'s role (OWNER or EDITOR). I\'m also planning a cohesive routing strategy in React to manage different views (Login, Register, Dashboard, etc.). I\'ll handle navigation and iframe constraints smoothly, using motion for transitions.\n\n\n**Defining Client-Device Relations**\n\nI am now focusing on the client-device relationship, defining the necessary fields: Name, CPF/CNPJ, Phone, Email, and Address for clients. For devices, I\'ll need Type (Computer, Printer, etc.), Brand, Model, and Serial Number. Validation for duplicate CPF/CNPJ entries is crucial, along with how to handle missing serial numbers. I\'ll need a way to display visual characteristics.\n\n**OS Creation and Receipt**\n\nMy focus has now shifted to creating the OS (Service Order) functionality at the `/ordens-servico` endpoint. This includes fields for Client, Device, Reported Defect, Left Accessories, and Equipment Condition. I need to generate unique, sequential OS numbers. I\'ll create a highly polished, view-only Service Receipt with a printable layout, a signature block, and visual details.\n\n**Kanban Board for Service Orders**\n\nI\'m now implementing a Kanban board view for Service Orders. Initial statuses will include \"Budget\" and \"Waiting for Parts.\"\n\n\n**Expanding Kanban Order Statuses**\n\nI\'m expanding the Kanban board view for Service Orders by adding \"Em Manuten\303\247\303\243o,\" \"Pronto para Retirada,\" and \"Finalizado\" statuses. I\'ll implement drag-and-drop functionality and quick status buttons using a PUT request to update the OS status. A technical detail panel on OS selection will display Diagn\303\263stico T\303\251cnico, Pe\303\247as Utilizadas (linked to local inventory), Pe\303\247as Custos/Valor do conserto, and Valor da M\303\243o de Obra, with a dynamically computed total.\n\n**Implementing Soft Delete**\n\nI am implementing a soft delete functionality using a `deletedAt` field for Clients, OS, and Devices. Role-based permissions are crucial; an `EDITOR` role should be forbidden from deleting OS or Clientes, returning a 403 error or displaying a visual block. The `OWNER` role will have deletion privileges.\n\n**Handling Frontend Connection Issues**\n\nMy focus has now shifted to frontend connection handling. I\'ll block drag-and-drop actions, show a visual disconnection indicator, and prevent API writes, warning the technician if the internet is lost or the offline simulation is enabled.\n\n\n**Integrating Bling and SEFAZ**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the integration with Bling and the Brazilian tax authority, SEFAZ. The goal is automated fiscal invoice generation upon Service Order completion. This includes handling data transfer to Bling\'s API with exponential backoff and circuit breakers for resilience. I\'ll also develop a comprehensive sandbox dashboard to simulate API requests and manage SEFAZ rejections, with an interactive status loading sequence.\n\n\n**Defining Printable OS Receipt**\n\nI\'m now generating a printer-friendly Service Receipt. I\'m focusing on layout, signature blocks, and visual elements. I\'m especially keen on creating a polished, professional output (including total value, tax details, and barcode) for the user to print or open.\n\nI\'m also creating the initial `src` directory structure, with global type definitions in `/src/types.ts`. I\'m defining `UserRole`, `User`, `Client`, and `Device` types and interfaces. I will need to handle file organization properly, so I will modularize our design to prevent the components from becoming enormous monolith files. I\'m creating mock and seed data in `/src/data.ts` to prime the system with test values.\n\n\n**Defining Data Types**\n\nI\'m now creating comprehensive type definitions in `/src/types.ts` for entities like `Device`, `OSStatus`, `Part`, `UsedPart`, and `OrdemServico`, which will underpin the data model and ensure type safety throughout the application. I\'m carefully considering all possible data relationships to build an accurate data-transfer interface.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 949783813
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
