  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Database Options**\n\nI\'m now focusing on database storage for the backend. I\'ve decided to initially implement a local JSON file, `/database.json`, which the Express server, `/server.ts`, will load and save. This provides persistence across development reloads, which is fantastic for rapid iteration.\n\n\n**Populating Database with Defaults**\n\nI\'m now populating the `/database.json` file. My goal is to pre-populate it with realistic data for a tech repair shop, like MGV Tecnologia, to streamline development. This includes initial users, customers, devices, parts inventory, and work orders in various stages. The key here is not to start with an empty database. I\'m choosing to pre-create the file to ensure the initial setup is consistent and robust.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 407993740
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
