  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Kanban Board Structure**\n\nI\'m incredibly impressed with the current setup. Now I am focused on the core Sprint 3 component, `src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx`. My current focus is defining its necessary Work Orders columns, including the \"Or\303\247amento (ORCAMENTO)\" and \"Aguardando Pe\303\247a (AGUARDANDO)\" stages.\n\n\n**Refining Kanban Column States**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the Kanban board\'s \"Work Order\" states. I\'ve expanded the state definition to include \"Em Manuten\303\247\303\243o,\" \"Pronto para Retirada,\" and \"Finalizado.\" Implementing drag-and-drop functionality is next, with a fallback UI control menu in case events are blocked. I\'m also planning the modal details for each OS, including dynamic cost calculations and inventory management; the modal will let us save changes. Network protection will block physical operations if offline.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
